<title>JAPAN: Japan Jan external reserves slip to $217.14 bln.</title>
<headline>Japan Jan external reserves slip to $217.14 bln.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's external reserves fell $731 million in January from a month earlier to $217.14 billion, the Ministry of Finance said on Monday.</p>
<p>Reserves had increased by $757 million in December to a record high of $217.87 billion. It was the 34th consecutive month in which the reserves had marked a record high. Figures may not tally due to rounding.</p>
</text>
